{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/925","id":4626672075,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQ8oa8s8AAAABE8Vpyw","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/925","diff_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/925.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/925.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/925","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/925/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/925/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/925/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/statuses/74e0970f0237fc5f3b02b19aa43e6b1c2ee3d1ea","number":925,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[I08:E00] GitHub library: one label per family, and a project field confirmed by re-read","user":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nThe library could add a label and could not replace the one label a family is supposed to hold. It also could not read or write a field on a project board. Board-driven work needs both, and a comment or a search could still put free text straight into the command.\n\n## What happens today\n\nAdding a label only appends. A family is the prefix before the first colon, as in `type:epic`, and the board convention keeps exactly one label in that family. Nothing in the library lists a project's fields or sets a single-select option. A comment body and an issue search were placed in the command itself, so a quote or a newline could end the value early.\n\n## The fix\n\n**Label family.** The library lists labels, removes one label, and replaces the label in a named family. Replacement deletes every other member of that family and reads the issue labels again. The result holds when exactly one label remains and it is the requested value.\n\n**Project fields.** The library finds a user-owned or organization-owned project, finds the item for an issue, reads a field (including each single-select option's id), and writes an option id. The write is confirmed by reading that option id back.\n\n**Free text.** A comment body and an issue search are written to a file and passed as a field.\n\n## Scope\n\nDefinitions on the workflows branch: the GitHub technique library, a conformance specimen that binds the new operations, and the four corpus-guard closures the sweep was already failing. No server source.\n\n## What was verified\n\nA live sidecar walk used throwaway user project 8 and issue 924. The family read showed only `throwaway:two`. The field read showed single-select option `29087cbe`.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo issue-type operations, no milestone operations, and no GraphQL.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-24T13:47:13Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T04:47:18Z","closed_at":"2026-09-24T14:25:55Z","merged_at":"2026-09-24T14:25:55Z","merge_commit_sha":"9b88a1f3162034629432fa4e23d2f9d39ddab151","assignee":null,"ass